     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi all,<div><br></div><div>Can lavaan output the degrees of freedom from the model statement <i>before</i> it runs a model?  I&#39;m trying to automate a bunch of simulations, and I don&#39;t want lavaan to try to estimate the models that don&#39;t have enough degrees of freedom.  I know that I could write my own function to compute this, but I figure there is no point in re-inventing the wheel (especially if someone already created a better one).</div><div><br></div><div>Melissa</div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Sat, Dec 19, 2020 at 6:38 PM &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">lav...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\">\r\n<div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(211,211,211);max-width:850px;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n  <div style=\"background-color:rgb(245,245,245);padding:10px 20px\">\r\n    <table cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"width:100%\">\r\n      <tbody>\r\n        <tr>\r\n          <td style=\"width:70%\">\r\n            <span style=\"font:18px/20px arial;color:rgb(51,51,51)\">\r\n              <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/forum/?utm_source=digest&amp;utm_medium=email#!forum/lavaan/topics\" style=\"text-decoration:none;color:rgb(51,51,51)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/forum/?utm_source%3Ddigest%26utm_medium%3Demail%23!forum/lavaan/topics&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792420010224000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2bxfRPjLuroSZJp5bFYKam\">\r\n              lav...@googlegroups.com</a>\r\n            </span>\r\n          </td>\r\n          <td style=\"text-align:right;width:30%\">\r\n            <span style=\"font:20px/24px arial\"><a style=\"color:rgb(221,75,57);text-decoration:none\" href=\"https://groups.google.com/forum/?utm_source=digest&amp;utm_medium=email/#!overview\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/forum/?utm_source%3Ddigest%26utm_medium%3Demail/%23!overview&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792420010224000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2QWKeT-erWSMU6glCwG--f\">Google Groups</a></span>\r\n          </td>\r\n          <td style=\"width:32px\">\r\n            <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/forum/?utm_source=digest&amp;utm_medium=email/#!overview\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/forum/?utm_source%3Ddigest%26utm_medium%3Demail/%23!overview&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792420010224000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2QWKeT-erWSMU6glCwG--f\"><img style=\"border:0px;vertical-align:middle\" src=\"https://ci5.googleusercontent.com/proxy/4SGWHe9midrWMDxDIJMQraTMMgnAU71soPZ0D28IOSZcs66TdyRoCqyIhaTt-kwo0YKv2lRo05RkwsGFZdnFhdvy60XdxNlL2U-B=s0-d-e1-ft#http://www.google.com/images/icons/product/groups-32.png\"></a>\r\n          </td>\r\n        </tr>\r\n      </tbody>\r\n    </table>\r\n  </div>\r\n  <div style=\"padding:20px;background-color:rgb(245,245,245)\">\r\n\r\n\r\n<div style=\"font-family:arial;color:rgb(34,34,34);padding:0px\">\r\n  <a name=\"m_-8385894934681789643_m_-4002603969199687397_digest_top\" style=\"font-size:21px\" rel=\"nofollow\">\r\n  \r\n    Today&#39;s topic summary\r\n  \r\n  \r\n  </a><br>\r\n  <span style=\"font-size:11px\">\r\n    <a style=\"color:rgb(17,85,204);text-decoration:none\" href=\"https://groups.google.com/forum/?utm_source=digest&amp;utm_medium=email#!forum/lavaan/topics\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/forum/?utm_source%3Ddigest%26utm_medium%3Demail%23!forum/lavaan/topics&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792420010224000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2bxfRPjLuroSZJp5bFYKam\">View all topics</a>\r\n  </span>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font:13px/18px arial;color:rgb(34,34,34);padding:0px;margin-bottom:30px\">\r\n  <ul style=\"margin-left:3px;padding-left:0px\">\r\n  \r\n    <li>\r\n      <a style=\"color:rgb(17,85,204);text-decoration:none\" href=\"#m_-8385894934681789643_m_-4002603969199687397_group_thread_0\" rel=\"nofollow\">\r\n      five Likert scale data that are not distributed in a normal distribution</a> -\r\n      <span style=\"color:rgb(119,119,119)\">7 Updates</span>\r\n    </li>\r\n  \r\n    <li>\r\n      <a style=\"color:rgb(17,85,204);text-decoration:none\" href=\"#m_-8385894934681789643_m_-4002603969199687397_group_thread_1\" rel=\"nofollow\">\r\n      Latent Growth Curve Model</a> -\r\n      <span style=\"color:rgb(119,119,119)\">1 Update</span>\r\n    </li>\r\n  \r\n  </ul>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n  \r\n  <a name=\"m_-8385894934681789643_m_-4002603969199687397_group_thread_0\" rel=\"nofollow\"></a>\r\n  <div style=\"display:inline-block;font-family:arial;padding:4px 0px 5px\">\r\n  \r\n    <a href=\"http://groups.google.com/group/lavaan/t/27b9062d3db39a9a?utm_source=digest&amp;utm_medium=email\" style=\"font-size:21px;color:rgb(17,85,204);text-decoration:none\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://groups.google.com/group/lavaan/t/27b9062d3db39a9a?utm_source%3Ddigest%26utm_medium%3Demail&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792420010224000&amp;usg=AOvVaw38w6G2f4VAbBciwhCKoMXa\">\r\n      five Likert scale data that are not distributed in a normal distribution\r\n    </a>\r\n  \r\n  </div>\r\n\r\n  <table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;width:100%\">\r\n    \r\n    <tbody><tr><td style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(46,46,46);font-family:arial;padding:10px 15px;border:1px solid rgb(211,211,211)\">\r\n      <span style=\"color:rgb(177,176,176);font-size:15px\">\r\n        Omar Salim &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">omarsal...@gmail.com</a>&gt;: Dec 19 03:23PM -0800\r\n      </span>\r\n      <br><br>\r\n      Hi<br>\r\nI have five Likert scale data that are not distributed in a normal <br>\r\ndistribution. Is there a method by Lavaan that can be converted to a normal <br>\r\ndistribution?<br>\r\nI noticed that some researchers\r\n      \r\n        <span style=\"font-size:11px\"><a style=\"color:rgb(17,85,204);text-decoration:none\" href=\"http://groups.google.com/group/lavaan/msg/33a4259e85f9f?utm_source=digest&amp;utm_medium=email\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://groups.google.com/group/lavaan/msg/33a4259e85f9f?utm_source%3Ddigest%26utm_medium%3Demail&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792420010224000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1nMitsBu9AlTap7SYsx7kW\">...more</a></span>\r\n        <br>\r\n      \r\n    </td></tr>\r\n    \r\n    <tr><td style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(46,46,46);font-family:arial;padding:10px 15px;border:1px solid rgb(211,211,211)\">\r\n      <span style=\"color:rgb(177,176,176);font-size:15px\">\r\n        &quot;Patrick (Malone Quantitative)&quot; &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">mal...@malonequantitative.com</a>&gt;: Dec 19 06:36PM -0500\r\n      </span>\r\n      <br><br>\r\n      For skewed, 5-point data, you need to use ordinal-data methods. Which<br>\r\nlavaan can do just fine.<br>\r\n <br>\r\n <br>\r\n-- <br>\r\nPatrick S. Malone, Ph.D., Malone Quantitative<br>\r\nNEW Service Models:\r\n      \r\n        <span style=\"font-size:11px\"><a style=\"color:rgb(17,85,204);text-decoration:none\" href=\"http://groups.google.com/group/lavaan/msg/33afa9e0d08f5?utm_source=digest&amp;utm_medium=email\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://groups.google.com/group/lavaan/msg/33afa9e0d08f5?utm_source%3Ddigest%26utm_medium%3Demail&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792420010224000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3Dwij_jO1meEf3mfMqXZ0h\">...more</a></span>\r\n        <br>\r\n      \r\n    </td></tr>\r\n    \r\n    <tr><td style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(46,46,46);font-family:arial;padding:10px 15px;border:1px solid rgb(211,211,211)\">\r\n      <span style=\"color:rgb(177,176,176);font-size:15px\">\r\n        Omar Salim &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">omarsal...@gmail.com</a>&gt;: Dec 20 02:53AM +0300\r\n      </span>\r\n      <br><br>\r\n      How do you have an example for converting data into a normal distribution<br>\r\n <br>\r\n‫في الأحد، 20 ديسمبر 2020 في 2:36 ص تمت كتابة ما يلي بواسطة ‪Patrick\r\n      \r\n        <span style=\"font-size:11px\"><a style=\"color:rgb(17,85,204);text-decoration:none\" href=\"http://groups.google.com/group/lavaan/msg/33beb7fd40526?utm_source=digest&amp;utm_medium=email\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://groups.google.com/group/lavaan/msg/33beb7fd40526?utm_source%3Ddigest%26utm_medium%3Demail&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792420010224000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0qnkWeW0fX3-If1TiVbSll\">...more</a></span>\r\n        <br>\r\n      \r\n    </td></tr>\r\n    \r\n    <tr><td style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(46,46,46);font-family:arial;padding:10px 15px;border:1px solid rgb(211,211,211)\">\r\n      <span style=\"color:rgb(177,176,176);font-size:15px\">\r\n        &quot;Patrick (Malone Quantitative)&quot; &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">mal...@malonequantitative.com</a>&gt;: Dec 19 06:56PM -0500\r\n      </span>\r\n      <br><br>\r\n      I&#39;m saying you shouldn&#39;t do that, even if you could.<br>\r\n <br>\r\n <br>\r\n-- <br>\r\nPatrick S. Malone, Ph.D., Malone Quantitative<br>\r\nNEW Service Models: <a href=\"http://malonequantitative.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://malonequantitative.com&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792420010224000&amp;usg=AOvVaw023GXxfnFxCWc1sz3vbF6W\">http://malonequantitative.com</a><br>\r\n <br>\r\nHe/Him/His<br>\r\n\r\n      \r\n        <span style=\"font-size:11px\"><a style=\"color:rgb(17,85,204);text-decoration:none\" href=\"http://groups.google.com/group/lavaan/msg/33c1947e3e4c9?utm_source=digest&amp;utm_medium=email\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://groups.google.com/group/lavaan/msg/33c1947e3e4c9?utm_source%3Ddigest%26utm_medium%3Demail&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792420010224000&amp;usg=AOvVaw39SqPYPfxBTJ0VDXfcRmul\">...more</a></span>\r\n        <br>\r\n      \r\n    </td></tr>\r\n    \r\n    <tr><td style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(46,46,46);font-family:arial;padding:10px 15px;border:1px solid rgb(211,211,211)\">\r\n      <span style=\"color:rgb(177,176,176);font-size:15px\">\r\n        &quot;Patrick (Malone Quantitative)&quot; &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">mal...@malonequantitative.com</a>&gt;: Dec 19 06:58PM -0500\r\n      </span>\r\n      <br><br>\r\n      The probit regression that lavaan uses with ordered data (outcomes or<br>\r\nindicators) assumes an underlying normal distribution that is coarsely<br>\r\nmeasured, at various cutpoints reflected by the\r\n      \r\n        <span style=\"font-size:11px\"><a style=\"color:rgb(17,85,204);text-decoration:none\" href=\"http://groups.google.com/group/lavaan/msg/33c2e0a830fd4?utm_source=digest&amp;utm_medium=email\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://groups.google.com/group/lavaan/msg/33c2e0a830fd4?utm_source%3Ddigest%26utm_medium%3Demail&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792420010224000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3EJPToGOO7GRbSsyls-p2a\">...more</a></span>\r\n        <br>\r\n      \r\n    </td></tr>\r\n    \r\n    <tr><td style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(46,46,46);font-family:arial;padding:10px 15px;border:1px solid rgb(211,211,211)\">\r\n      <span style=\"color:rgb(177,176,176);font-size:15px\">\r\n        <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">car...@web.de</a>: Dec 20 02:10AM +0100\r\n      </span>\r\n      <br><br>\r\n      Although this is often (rightly) discussed critically, you could consider scales with 5 points as continuous and use MLR. A transformation of the data makes little sense. Pat has already noted this.\r\n      \r\n        <span style=\"font-size:11px\"><a style=\"color:rgb(17,85,204);text-decoration:none\" href=\"http://groups.google.com/group/lavaan/msg/340200c5b299f?utm_source=digest&amp;utm_medium=email\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://groups.google.com/group/lavaan/msg/340200c5b299f?utm_source%3Ddigest%26utm_medium%3Demail&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792420010224000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0lL11tDRzTEQfAS5Bze5nP\">...more</a></span>\r\n        <br>\r\n      \r\n    </td></tr>\r\n    \r\n    <tr><td style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(46,46,46);font-family:arial;padding:10px 15px;border:1px solid rgb(211,211,211)\">\r\n      <span style=\"color:rgb(177,176,176);font-size:15px\">\r\n        &quot;Patrick (Malone Quantitative)&quot; &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">mal...@malonequantitative.com</a>&gt;: Dec 19 09:36PM -0500\r\n      </span>\r\n      <br><br>\r\n      What I see as conventional wisdom is 5 points is usually enough if it&#39;s<br>\r\nsymmetric. I&#39;m not sure it wouldn&#39;t be overtaxing MLR to apply to discrete<br>\r\nand skewed concurrently.<br>\r\n <br>\r\n\r\n      \r\n        <span style=\"font-size:11px\"><a style=\"color:rgb(17,85,204);text-decoration:none\" href=\"http://groups.google.com/group/lavaan/msg/344c92e7d3ff2?utm_source=digest&amp;utm_medium=email\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://groups.google.com/group/lavaan/msg/344c92e7d3ff2?utm_source%3Ddigest%26utm_medium%3Demail&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792420010224000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2k3yUtbxnCyrGw-x6ZuvUK\">...more</a></span>\r\n        <br>\r\n      \r\n    </td></tr>\r\n    \r\n  </tbody></table>\r\n  <div style=\"font-size:11px;margin-bottom:40px;margin-top:5px\">\r\n    <a style=\"color:rgb(17,85,204);text-decoration:none\" href=\"#m_-8385894934681789643_m_-4002603969199687397_digest_top\" rel=\"nofollow\">Back to top</a>\r\n  </div>\r\n\r\n\r\n  \r\n  <a name=\"m_-8385894934681789643_m_-4002603969199687397_group_thread_1\" rel=\"nofollow\"></a>\r\n  <div style=\"display:inline-block;font-family:arial;padding:4px 0px 5px\">\r\n  \r\n    <a href=\"http://groups.google.com/group/lavaan/t/74d2d735a4458730?utm_source=digest&amp;utm_medium=email\" style=\"font-size:21px;color:rgb(17,85,204);text-decoration:none\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://groups.google.com/group/lavaan/t/74d2d735a4458730?utm_source%3Ddigest%26utm_medium%3Demail&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792420010224000&amp;usg=AOvVaw090uRrPM52zz9VpUkYVSa0\">\r\n      Latent Growth Curve Model\r\n    </a>\r\n  \r\n  </div>\r\n\r\n  <table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;width:100%\">\r\n    \r\n    <tbody><tr><td style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(46,46,46);font-family:arial;padding:10px 15px;border:1px solid rgb(211,211,211)\">\r\n      <span style=\"color:rgb(177,176,176);font-size:15px\">\r\n        Mauricio Garnier-Villarreal &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">mauga...@gmail.com</a>&gt;: Dec 19 04:10PM -0800\r\n      </span>\r\n      <br><br>\r\n      Manuel<br>\r\n <br>\r\nI took these constriant out, because you dont need to constraint interceots <br>\r\nuntil you are in the string invariance model. I dont see why these <br>\r\nconstraints are there for the configural\r\n      \r\n        <span style=\"font-size:11px\"><a style=\"color:rgb(17,85,204);text-decoration:none\" href=\"http://groups.google.com/group/lavaan/msg/33cd2262f047b?utm_source=digest&amp;utm_medium=email\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://groups.google.com/group/lavaan/msg/33cd2262f047b?utm_source%3Ddigest%26utm_medium%3Demail&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792420010224000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2axf9CMtuTKsQgHuVxzHv6\">...more</a></span>\r\n        <br>\r\n      \r\n    </td></tr>\r\n    \r\n  </tbody></table>\r\n  <div style=\"font-size:11px;margin-bottom:40px;margin-top:5px\">\r\n    <a style=\"color:rgb(17,85,204);text-decoration:none\" href=\"#m_-8385894934681789643_m_-4002603969199687397_digest_top\" rel=\"nofollow\">Back to top</a>\r\n  </div>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n  </div>\r\n  <div style=\"background-color:rgb(245,245,245);padding:5px 20px\">\r\n  <table cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"width:100%\">\r\n  <tbody><tr>\r\n    <td style=\"padding-top:4px;font-family:arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(99,99,99);font-size:11px\">\r\n      \r\n      You received this digest because you&#39;re subscribed to updates for this group. You can change your settings on the <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/forum/?utm_source=digest&amp;utm_medium=email#!forum/lavaan/join\" style=\"color:rgb(17,85,204);text-decoration:none\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/forum/?utm_source%3Ddigest%26utm_medium%3Demail%23!forum/lavaan/join&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792420010224000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1t5M_0_jehkzU_KzIHS41r\">group membership page</a>.<br>\r\n      To unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it send an email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">lavaan+un...@googlegroups.com</a>.\r\n    </td>\r\n  </tr></tbody>\r\n  </table>\r\n  </div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n</blockquote></div><br clear=\"all\"><div><br></div>-- <br><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_signature\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Melissa Gordon Wolf<div><a href=\"http://www.melissagwolf.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.melissagwolf.com&amp;source=gmail&amp;u