    [
     1,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div>You can pass your syntax to<font face=\"Courier New\"> lavaanify() </font>to convert it to a parameter table, then pass that to the utility function<font face=\"Courier New\"> lav_partable_df()</font>.  Note that you must either specify all free parameters in your model syntax, or tell<font face=\"Courier New\"> lavaanify() </font>to automatically free parameters that wrappers like<font face=\"Courier New\"> cfa() </font>and<font face=\"Courier New\"> sem() </font>do, using the <font face=\"Courier New\">auto* </font>arguments.  For example:</div><div><br></div><div><font face=\"Courier New\">example(cfa) # df = 24</font></div><div><font face=\"Courier New\">lav_partable_df(lavaanify(HS.model, auto = TRUE)) # 24</font><br></div><div><br></div><div><div><div>Terrence D. Jorgensen</div><div>Assistant Professor, Methods and Statistics</div><div>Research Institute for Child Development and Education, the University of Amsterdam</div><div><a href=\"http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792420010225000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0ltBQxbPhbbuU03Sk-60PI\">http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen</a></div></div><div><br></div><div></div></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
